  - elementId: highlight-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [660, 420, 560, 100]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: highlight-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [680, 430, 520, 80]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p><strong>Graph lift: +0.131</strong> (uniform_graph − no_graph)</p>
        <p style="margin-top:4px">Validated by synthetic control: no lift on independent zones. The gain is real cross-zonal coupling.</p>
  - elementId: bottom-note
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 560, 1160, 50]
    content:
      fontSize: 14
      color: "$darkGray"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        <p>Attention improves ranking (rank-IC 0.612 vs 0.584) but is a wash on MSE skill — uniform pooling is near MSE-optimal on this graph. Echoes the equity finding: attention's value is a modest tilt on broad pooling.</p>
